## Web research

When you need current information (library APIs, CVEs, recent best practices), use a web-search MCP (e.g. Perplexity) over guessing from memory. Send the full question with context, not bare keywords.

## NPM package documentation

Before using an unfamiliar npm package:

1. Resolve the library ID via the Context7 MCP (`resolve-library-id`).
2. Fetch the docs (`get-library-docs`) for the resolved ID.
3. Combine with a focused web search if the docs are thin.

Read the package's interface BEFORE writing code that calls it. Do not fabricate APIs.
